%%pianopath variantOf=song.folk.exercise-cielito-lindo.pdmx variantLabel="simple, one note in the left hand"
%%pianopath editionNotes="A simplification. The right hand is the melody note for note and tie for tie as the PDMX edition 'Exercise - Cielito Lindo' writes it, in quarter notes; a lead-sheet edition (CID QmPbR5ngH5hsCGjDz7bZJTxRgSAp1tiPyh8Rrjrj4yjDWB) writes the same tune with the same ties but one, a few bars decorated in eighths, and gives the chords. The left hand plays each bar's chord root from that lead sheet, one held note in C position. Every tie is the tune's own long note carried over the bar line. The fingering is marked at every move of the right hand; the teaching tempo is the arranger's, and the song is usually sung much faster."
